  {
    "number": 214,
    "title": "Use shared npm and Playwright caches in setup guidance",
    "body": "Refs #212\n\n## Summary\n\n`docs/development.md` (Workflow commands): replaces \"For a WSL sandbox with a read-only npm cache, use a writable temporary cache.\" with guidance to use npm's and Playwright's default caches. These are `~/.npm` and `~/.cache/ms-playwright` on Linux and WSL. A read-only cache gets reported instead of redirected, because `/tmp` can be a small RAM-backed filesystem shared by every session.\n\n## Why\n\nOn 2026-09-23 the WSL host's RAM-backed `/tmp` filled completely, partly from caches and per-task installs placed there. The Codex local-development sandbox profile now allows writes to both default caches, so the temporary-cache workaround is no longer needed. The same change landed in codex-nanoleaf (#85) and divoom-app-upgrade (#73).\n\nThis is also the first non-guide change after #211 (Refs #210). Its PR and merged-main Work guide jobs are therefore the Depot evidence for #210, and for #207, whose main Work guide job failed on the old clipboard check.\n\n## Candidate evidence\n\n- Base: `146602fccea5dc77e6731a84826e507f62c5bf8a` (origin/main, includes #211). Head: `726f09986c4517e56e9c78e819c7fb484a51a470`. Merge-base: the base.\n- Diff: `git diff 146602fccea5dc77e6731a84826e507f62c5bf8a...726f09986c4517e56e9c78e819c7fb484a51a470` (`docs/development.md` only). Worktree clean at head.\n- Validation at head with Node v24.21.0 through `fnm exec --using=.nvmrc --`: `npm ci` exit 0; `npm run check:workflow` exit 0 (15 of 15 items valid, inventory unchanged); `npm run test:workflow` exit 0 (15 of 15).\n- Out of scope: examples that write a single small report file under `/tmp` (for example the compatibility report path) stay, as #212 states.\n\n## Scope notes\n\nDocumentation only; no product behavior, OpenSpec or UI change. Paths are outside `docs/work-guide/`, so normal Depot CI applies, including the Work guide job.\n\n## Reviews\n\nIndependent Standards and Specification reviews pending.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
    "state": "open",
